  <data name="AnalysisAboutValuesDescription.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>RGB curves come from scRGB preview after display mapping. The left half is SDR (sRGB encoded scale) with center line as current SDR white point; each dashed line in the right half adds +1 EV of exposure, with the far right holding +6 EV and above. All three channels share the vertical axis using square root of pixel count to preserve small peaks. Negative channel values clamp to the far left. Bottom luminance readings are RGB weighted luminance, not screen measurements. Split-screen line is excluded. Refresh after zooming, navigating, or changing display settings. Right side of split screen uses adaptive HDR.</value>
